{"id": "EUVD-2026-97581", "enisaUuid": "ee61dbca-021d-37a6-988b-cada7d52dabd", "description": "ImageMagick before 6.9.13-57 and 7.x before 7.1.2-32 lacks proper synchronization when the security policy is accessed, so simultaneous reads and writes of the policy by multiple threads trigger a race condition that causes a heap buffer over-write. An attacker able to induce concurrent security policy access can crash the application, causing a denial of service.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:04:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T16:55:48", "baseScore": 2.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-8x3v-wr32-qqh4", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/12db6f04e895deae4537ead10c771a244607794a", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/9ddc71abea5cbe7d18164fa0f0077a105cab514f", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/imagemagick-before-6.9.13-57-and-7-x-before-7.1.2-32-heap-buffer-overflow-via-concurrent-security-policy-access"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109279", "GHSA-xg3c-hhwj-7xrg"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.09, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "819f4555-80b9-3d81-b4a2-c4d406b8c5e8", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.9.13-57"}, {"id": "c98a96f2-9d7c-3fea-8c52-7ff82b5725bb", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "7.0.0-0 <7.1.2-32"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a3256618-de64-3c16-85f2-dfe320369b0c", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}], "isExploited": false}